`buildMongoEnums` or `MongoEnumAccessors`.\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/extension/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.21-to-8.0.0-rc.22/instructions.md:const driverInstance = clientStack.driver.create();\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/extension/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.21-to-8.0.0-rc.22/instructions.md:const driver = stack.driver.create();\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/extension/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.21-to-8.0.0-rc.22/instructions.md:Replace `MongoDriverImpl.fromDb(client.db(dbName))` with `driver.connect({ kind: 'mongoClient', client, dbName })` on a driver created the same way. Code that only sends DDL through a control adapter can use the control driver instead: `await mongoControlDriver.create(url)`, with `mongoControlDriver` the default export of `@prisma/orm-target-mongo/driver/control`. The control driver uses the database the URL names, so put `dbName` in the URL's path, for example `mongodb://localhost:27017/app`.\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/extension/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.21-to-8.0.0-rc.22/instructions.md:const runtime = createMongoRuntime({ context, adapter: stack.adapter.create(stack), driver });\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/app/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.18-to-8.0.0-rc.19/instructions.md:      On a client that closes at once (`postgres({ contract, url })`, `sqlite()`, `supabase()`), an ORM call that resolves to one value, such as `first()`, `create()`, `include(...).create()` or a nested create, starts when it is called, and `close()` waits for it, so one left pending at `close()` now completes instead of rejecting: a `create()` used to reject with \"Runtime is closed\", and `include(...).create()` and a nested create with \"Postgres client is closed\". A streaming read such as `all()` starts when it is read; read after `close()`, it rejects with \"Postgres client is closed\" instead of \"Runtime is closed\". Update code or tests that expect the old outcome.\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/app/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.18-to-8.0.0-rc.19/instructions.md:await db.orm.public.Post.create({ title: 'Hello', publishedAt: new Date() as unknown as string });\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/app/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.18-to-8.0.0-rc.19/instructions.md:await db.orm.public.Post.create({ title: 'Hello', publishedAt: new Date().toISOString() });\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/app/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.18-to-8.0.0-rc.19/instructions.md:- await db.orm.User.create({ id: '123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000' as Char<36>, email });\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/app/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.18-to-8.0.0-rc.19/instructions.md:+ await db.orm.User.create({ id: '123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000', email });\nnode_modules/@prisma/orm-postgres/skills/prisma-8/upgrading/app/upgrades/8.0.0-rc.18-to-8.0.0-rc.19/instructions.md:const user = await db.orm.users.create({ name: 'Alice' });\n    Post: Models.public_Post;\n    User: Models.public_User;\n            readonly Post: {\n            readonly User: {\n    readonly Post: { readonly namespace: 'public' & NamespaceId; readonly model: 'Post' };\n    readonly User: { readonly namespace: 'public' & NamespaceId; readonly model: 'User' };\n          readonly Post: {\n          readonly User: {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
